// Telosmith records. Append-only: add a new version instead of editing a line.
{"id": "AU-owner", "version": 1, "type": "authority", "text": "Zach Rhodes: design intent and acceptance", "governs": ["purpose", "design", "acceptance", "code"]}
{"id": "P0", "version": 1, "type": "purpose", "subject": "purpose", "owner": "AU-owner", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "TODO: the owner states what this project is for (stub from aec init)"}
{"id": "P0", "version": 2, "type": "purpose", "subject": "purpose", "owner": "AU-owner", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:abi", "text": "Evaluate and improve crank-mem (Chris Liva) safely: overhaul, improve, integrate, and give it a better one-click install, as a private evaluation copy whose changes are offered upstream on the author's terms.", "source": "Zach 2026-11-10: \"Can we also look at ChrisLiva/crank-mem and A) overhaul B) improve C) integrate. Even just better 1-click install would be nice\"", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "P0@1"}]}
{"id": "AS-license", "version": 1, "type": "assumption", "authored_by": "claude:abi", "text": "Upstream declares no license at 2d72f6c, so all rights stay with Chris Liva; this copy stays private and is credited in ATTRIBUTION.md."}
{"id": "R-consolidation-input", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:abi", "text": "Consolidation gives the model no file tools: crank-mem selects cited files, admits each only if it is inside the project by real path, not sensitive by either name in any case, not hidden, regular and within size, and sends redacted, line-numbered excerpts marked as data. Uncited proposals are not accepted.", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AS-license@1"}]}
{"id": "R-consolidation-switch", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:abi", "text": "Consolidation has its own switch, off by default; turning digests on does not turn consolidation on.", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-index-containment", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:abi", "text": "Nothing outside the project by real path is indexed or read: every index and read path passes one shared gate (real-path containment, sensitivity on requested and resolved names, regular file).", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-monorepo-git", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:abi", "text": "A project rooted in a repository subdirectory honours the enclosing repository: its listing respects .gitignore, exclude mode writes to the enclosing repository's exclude file, and a git failure inside a repository keeps the previous index rather than walking unfiltered.", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-installer", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:abi", "text": "A guided one-command install: small core by default (dashboard and model optional), Claude/Codex/both selection, preview of every config change, resumable or reversible after interruption, safe repeat, upgrade and uninstall, consolidation off and Codex trust review on by default.", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "D-consolidation-optionA", "version": 1, "type": "decision", "subject": "design", "status": "accepted", "decided_by": "AU-owner", "authored_by": "claude:abi", "text": "Adopt the excerpt-only consolidation design (Option A in PROPOSAL.md) for this copy.", "source": "Zach 2026-11-10: \"Sounds good to me!\" after the excerpt-only explanation", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "R-consolidation-input@1"}]}
{"id": "AM-anamnesis-adapter", "version": 1, "type": "ambition", "owner": "AU-owner", "authored_by": "claude:abi", "text": "A versioned read-only search/export adapter on one non-sensitive repo, with Anamnesis keeping cross-project memory and authority. Not adopted.", "source": "Abigail assignment 2026-11-10"}
{"id": "E-suite-2026-11-10", "version": 1, "type": "evidence", "tier": "observed", "evidence_kind": "contract_conformance", "method": "bun test (bun 1.4.4, Linux sandbox, HOME/CRANK_HOME isolated)", "authored_by": "claude:abi", "text": "Full suite after 8b537c1: 821 pass / 47 fail, versus 806 / 47 at 2d72f6c; the 47 failures are the same set at both commits (search model not downloaded, running as root, sandbox Bun cache in test projects). The 15 new tests pass, and each fix's key tests fail when its fix is removed.", "limits": "One environment; macOS, Windows and node runtimes not run; no live Claude Code call; the 47 environmental failures hide whatever those tests would show here.", "relations": [{"rel": "supports", "to": "R-index-containment@1"}, {"rel": "supports", "to": "R-monorepo-git@1"}, {"rel": "supports", "to": "R-consolidation-input@1"}, {"rel": "supports", "to": "R-consolidation-switch@1"}]}
{"id": "D-installer-build", "version": 1, "type": "decision", "subject": "design", "status": "accepted", "decided_by": "AU-owner", "authored_by": "claude:abi", "text": "Build the guided one-command installer, doctor and safely re-runnable setup.", "source": "Zach 2026-11-10: \"I'd like the one-click installer doctor command safe rerunnable setup to be built. Yes.\"", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "R-installer@1"}]}
{"id": "D-two-branches", "version": 1, "type": "decision", "subject": "purpose", "status": "accepted", "decided_by": "AU-owner", "authored_by": "claude:abi", "text": "Keep two branches: one carrying Telosmith records, and one that does not require Telosmith, to offer back to Chris Liva.", "source": "Zach 2026-11-10: \"two branches, one with telosmith, one that does not require telosmith. I want to send this back to Chris as look at what I can do.\"", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AS-license@1"}]}
{"id": "E-suite-2026-11-10b", "version": 1, "type": "evidence", "tier": "observed", "evidence_kind": "contract_conformance", "method": "bun test, bun 1.4.4, Linux sandbox, fresh temporary HOME, run once at a18ef17 and once at 2d72f6c in a worktree", "authored_by": "claude:abi", "text": "At a18ef17: 859 pass / 29 fail; at 2d72f6c: 824 pass / 29 fail; the 29 failures are the identical set (search model not downloaded; running as root defeats the permission tests). 35 new tests, all passing. install.sh also ran end to end with a real `setup --core`, then init and doctor through the installed command.", "limits": "Linux only; macOS (BSD mv -h path, APFS case-insensitivity) and Windows untested; no live Claude Code session; installer tests run offline with the setup step replaced.", "relations": [{"rel": "supports", "to": "R-installer@1"}, {"rel": "supports", "to": "R-index-containment@1"}, {"rel": "supports", "to": "R-monorepo-git@1"}, {"rel": "supports", "to": "R-consolidation-input@1"}, {"rel": "supports", "to": "R-consolidation-switch@1"}]}
{"id": "AM-kairos-integration", "version": 1, "type": "ambition", "owner": "AU-owner", "epistemic": "inferred", "authored_by": "claude:kairos-coord", "text": "Integrate this copy into Kairos the way the other Kairos repos are: Telosmith active (hook and aec workflow, not just snippets), Lydian shared CI (records profile, since Lydian runs Python unittest only and this repo is TypeScript), and its own bun CI. Later, and only as a labelled trial: crank-mem as the per-repository session memory for one non-sensitive Kairos repo worked by Claude Code lanes, with Anamnesis keeping cross-project memory and authority (AM-anamnesis-adapter) and relay-kit keeping decisions and handoffs. crank-mem memory is never a decision record.", "source": "Zach 2026-11-11 15:38 CT: \"Let's begin to integrate crank-mem, including Telosmith and Lydian. You may infer purposes and intentions, as I am not sure\"", "rationale": "Inferred by the coordinator from P0@2, AM-anamnesis-adapter and how Kairos repos are set up; Zach asked for inference and may restate it."}
{"id": "R-branch-scope", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "inferred", "authored_by": "claude:kairos-coord", "text": "Kairos integration (Telosmith activation, Lydian, Kairos CI) lands only on main, the Telosmith branch. The proposed-changes branch stays free of Telosmith and Kairos machinery, so it remains a clean offer to Chris Liva.", "relations": [{"rel": "implements", "to": "D-two-branches@1"}], "rationale": "D-two-branches: one branch with Telosmith, one that does not require it."}
{"id": "AS-license", "version": 2, "type": "assumption", "epistemic": "contested", "authored_by": "claude:kairos-coord", "text": "Upstream declared no license at 2d72f6c, so all rights stay with Chris Liva; this copy is credited in ATTRIBUTION.md. Version 1 said the copy stays private, but the repository is public (it went public on 2026-11-10). Whether a public copy of unlicensed code is acceptable without Chris Liva's permission is open: Zach decides, or Chris Liva grants a license.", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "AS-license@1"}]}
{"id": "R-branch-scope", "version": 2, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "inferred", "authored_by": "claude:kairos-coord", "text": "Kairos integration (Telosmith activation, Lydian, Kairos CI) lands only on main, the Telosmith branch. The proposed-changes branch stays free of Telosmith and Kairos machinery, so it remains a clean offer to Chris Liva.", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "D-two-branches@1"}, {"rel": "supersedes", "to": "R-branch-scope@1"}], "rationale": "v2 only replaces the deprecated implements relation with serves."}
